-- title:
--   Smoothness of the two-chart integral model over its base
-- statement:
--   Let $R$ be a commutative ring, $F$ a field equipped with an $R$-algebra structure, and $j \in F$ a nonzero element. Write $A_{\mathrm{fin}} =$ `chartAlgFin R F j` for the $R$-subalgebra of $F$ consisting of those elements of $F$ that are integral over the $R$-subalgebra of $F$ generated by $j$, and $A_{\mathrm{inf}} =$ `chartAlgInf R F j` for the $R$-subalgebra of those elements integral over the $R$-subalgebra generated by $j^{-1}$; thus each chart algebra is the integral closure in $F$ of the corresponding adjoined subalgebra. The scheme `TwoChartIntegralModel R F j` is the pushout of the two morphisms $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the inclusions of $A_{\mathrm{fin}}$ and of $A_{\mathrm{inf}}$ into the middle algebra, and `toBase R F j` is the morphism to $\operatorname{Spec} R$ obtained from the universal property of that pushout out of the two structure morphisms $\operatorname{Spec}(R \to A_{\mathrm{fin}})$ and $\operatorname{Spec}(R \to A_{\mathrm{inf}})$. The assertion is that this morphism `toBase R F j` is smooth if and only if both $A_{\mathrm{fin}}$ and $A_{\mathrm{inf}}$ are smooth $R$-algebras in the sense of `Algebra.Smooth`.
--
--   This is the translation between smoothness of the two-chart integral model as a morphism of schemes and smoothness of its two chart rings as $R$-algebras. It is used in both directions in the construction of integral models of modular curves, for instance by [`ModularCurve.XOne.smooth_toBase_and_isIntegral_pullback_twoChartIntegralModel_x1`](thm.html#ModularCurve.XOne.smooth_toBase_and_isIntegral_pullback_twoChartIntegralModel_x1) and by the results on $\Gamma_0$-level Laurent base changes that deduce smoothness of relative dimension one, or uniqueness of a valuation subring, from ring-level input.
